// Frankenbuild SQ2 patch for Blender 5.2 - source/blender/gpu/opengl/gl_backend.cc
// Target: allow GUI on Qualcomm 8cx Gen2 / SQ1/SQ2 (Adreno 685/690, driver < 30.0.3820)
// Tradeoff: EEVEE Next + GPU Cycles OFF, Workbench/Solid + CPU Cycles ON.
// File IO for latest .blend files is CPU-only, so it keeps working.
//
// --- What upstream does (v4.2.19 gl_backend.cc, same in 5.x):
//
//   if (!(epoxy_gl_version() >= 43)) {
//     support_level = GPU_SUPPORT_LEVEL_UNSUPPORTED;
//   ...
//   // Any Qualcomm driver older than 30.x will never be capable of running blender >= 4.0
//   // As due to an issue in D3D typed UAV load capabilities, Compute Shaders are not available
//   // 30.0.3820.x and above ... only available on 8cx gen3 devices or newer
//   if (ver0 < 30 || (ver0 == 30 && ver1 == 0 && ver2 < 3820)) {
//     cout << "Qualcomm drivers older than 30.0.3820.x are not capable of running Blender 4.0\n"
//          << "If your device is older than an 8cx Gen3, you must use a 3.x LTS release.\n"
//     support_level = GPU_SUPPORT_LEVEL_UNSUPPORTED;
//   }
//
//   // SSBO check: max_ssbo_binds < 12 => UNSUPPORTED
//
// --- SQ2 patch (apply by hand, line numbers shift between 5.2/5.3):
//
// 1. In GLBackend::platform_init(), comment out the epoxy_gl_version() >= 43 hard fail.
//    Replace with: allow 42, mark as LIMITED, force workarounds on.
//    This gets you past the "Unsupported Graphics Card Configuration" dialog.
//
// 2. In the Qualcomm driver version block, delete the early UNSUPPORTED return for ver < 30.0.3820.
//    Replace with:
//      if (ver0 < 30 || (ver0 == 30 && ver1 == 0 && ver2 < 3820)) {
//        // SQ2 Frankenbuild: keep going, but kill compute-dependent paths.
//        GCaps.shader_draw_parameters_support = false;
//        GLContext::shader_draw_parameters_support = false;
//        GLContext::multi_draw_indirect_support = false;
//        // Force the same path as --debug-gpu-force-workarounds:
//        GCaps.hdr_viewport_support = false;
//        GLContext::clear_texture_support = false;
//        GLContext::multi_bind_support = false;
//        GLContext::multi_bind_image_support = false;
//        GLContext::direct_state_access_support = false;
//        GLContext::texture_filter_anisotropic_support = false;
//        GCaps.stencil_export_support = false;
//        GCaps.clip_control_support = false;
//        GLContext::layered_rendering_support = false;
//        support_level = GPU_SUPPORT_LEVEL_LIMITED; // NOT unsupported
//      }
//
// 3. In capabilities_init(), after the Qualcomm Mesa < 24 workaround that already disables
//    shader_draw_parameters, also force:
//      GLContext::multi_draw_indirect_support = false;
//    This avoids the multi-draw-indirect path that needs base-instance reads (broken on Gen2).
//
// 4. Build with EEVEE Next disabled for viewport, Workbench default:
//    - Preferences startup: Solid shading, not Material Preview / Rendered.
//    - Do NOT enable Vulkan backend (--gpu-backend OPENGL only).
//    - Cycles: CPU only. GPU Cycles on Adreno was never available on Windows ARM anyway.
//
// --- What this will and won't give you:
//
// WILL: Blender 5.2 GUI opens natively on SQ2 at hardware D3D12 speed for Solid/Wireframe
//       modeling, Outliner, UV, Graph editors, and latest .blend file IO (that's CPU code).
//       That's strictly better than WARP/llvmpipe software rasterizer (which you said is too slow)
//       because it keeps the Adreno D3D12 path for simple draws.
//
// WON'T: EEVEE Material Preview / Rendered viewport, EEVEE renders, or any compute-shader
//        feature (subdiv compute, some modifiers accelerated paths). Those need D3D typed UAV
//        loads that Gen2 drivers physically don't expose. They will render black / crash -
//        keep them off. Use Cycles CPU for final renders (your headless path already proves this works).
//
// --- Why 3.6 worked and 5.2 doesn't:
//
// Blender 4.0 raised minimum GL to 4.3 for Linux/Windows and EEVEE was rewritten (EEVEE Next)
// to require compute + SSBO>=12 + shader_draw_parameters + clip_control. 3.6 only needed GL 3.3
// paths your Gen2 Mesa GLOn12 (max ~4.2) can provide. This patch carves the 3.6-class GPU path
// back into the 5.2 codebase for the viewport only.
//
// Full build docs: https://developer.blender.org/docs/handbook/building_blender/
// Use prebuilt libs (don't rebuild deps): make update + `make lite` first, then full.
// Expected: ~100GB disk, VS2022 ARM64, 3-10 hrs on a faster machine - don't build ON the SQ2.
